# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_owner.py" "COCHANGE OWNER GATE: PASS" "co-change table OWNER (managed-PG deploy: the SECURITY DEFINER fns must OWN co_change or uninstall-purge/GDPR-erase/the 2nd detector break)" "co-change OWNER: on the MANAGED-Postgres deploy path (the schema applied by a role that is a MEMBER of veripsa_migrator -- GRANT veripsa_migrator TO <owner> then apply AS <owner>, OUR Render prod per render.yaml) Postgres makes a freshly-CREATEd table owned by the CURRENT role (<owner>), NOT the role it is a member of. core.co_change + core.co_change_seen_commit were the ONLY core tables MISSING the post-CREATE 'ALTER TABLE ... OWNER TO veripsa_migrator' that 20_core.sql gives every other core table (claim/code_node/code_edge/graph_version/event/intent), so on that path they ended up owned by <owner> while the 5 SECURITY DEFINER fns that touch them run AS veripsa_migrator -> every one hit 'permission denied for table co_change': purge_account_working_set_with_authority (uninstall) SILENTLY no-ops (the 'we purge on uninstall' privacy claim BROKEN), erase_account_with_authority (GDPR Art.17/CCPA) RAISES (a 'delete ALL my data' request FAILS), and ingest/filter/partners/all (the co-change 2nd detector) die SILENTLY (fail-open in the App). The rest of the suite MISSED it because bootstrap_local.sh/run_gates apply the schema AS veripsa_migrator directly, so the table owner is already correct and the missing ALTER is a no-op. This gate applies the schema AS A veripsa_migrator-MEMBER owner (the bug-reproducing condition the suite lacked) and asserts the AFTER-fix reality: (1) co_change + co_change_seen_commit are owned by veripsa_migrator (with a control on claim, which always had the OWNER line, to prove the harness is sound); (2) the DEFINER fns FUNCTION as the App -- ingest + read-back-all + partner read + filter-unseen all succeed, and a re-delivered push is a true sha-deduped no-op; (3) the uninstall purge returns ok:true AND actually DELETES the co_change rows (privacy honored, not a silent no-op); (4) the GDPR erase returns ok:true AND its deletion receipt counts the co_change rows deleted (complete); (5) MOAT INTACT -- a non-App raw INSERT is STILL forgery-refused (owning the table did not weaken the governed-write wall). The fix is idempotent + migration-safe: a member CAN reassign to a role it is a member of, and re-applying the schema REASSIGNS an already-mis-owned table, so a PO-gated prod REDEPLOY repairs the LIVE managed deploy in place. Content-free throughout (paths + counts only); apply-to-prod is PO-gated (additive DDL)" "co-change OWNER: the two co-change tables are reassigned to veripsa_migrator after CREATE (mirroring 20_core.sql) so the uninstall-purge / GDPR-erase / co-change 2nd-detector SECURITY DEFINER fns FUNCTION on the managed-PG member-owner deploy path -- proven by applying the schema AS a veripsa_migrator-member and exercising purge (deletes co_change, ok:true) + erase (receipt counts co_change) + ingest/read/filter (alive), with the governed-write moat still refusing a non-App write; content-free" 20
